From 10efccd68f854a761ab9e4c6d73a924d7d8a9e27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:47:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Take the pointer position from wl_pointer.enter

The enter handler was empty, so cur_x/cur_y were only set by motion. A
stylus or touchscreen driving wl_pointer makes the compositor jump the
pointer onto the surface, so a tap arrives as enter, button press,
button release with no motion in between. The press then saw
cur_x < 0 and was dropped. A real iPAQ session shows it: enter(83.9, 57.5)
followed by a press and release, and no key sent.

Move the position bookkeeping (enter, leave, motion, whether a position
is known, and the target of a press) into pointer.c, which has no
Wayland in it, and record the position from enter. Enter is ignored
while the keyboard is not mapped, like motion. An enter while the button
is held hands the held key over the way motion does.

tests/test-pointer.c covers the tap after enter, after leave, a press
with no position, motion, leave and a held button.
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
